# source: spec
# spec: docs/protocol/ni-framing.md#dispatcher-frames
# provenance: PV-0001, PV-0002, PV-0003, PV-0007, PV-0204
# kind: ni-stream
# description: A **DPTMOPC** dispatcher frame is an ordinary NI frame of length 17: the 12-byte literal plus 5 further bytes.
# derivation: u32 BE length 17 (PV-0001..PV-0003, PV-0204), then the literal of PV-0007 and 5 bytes whose content is unknown (gap #3), here arbitrary.
# expect.frames: 1
# expect.frame.1.offset: 4
# expect.frame.1.length: 17
# expect.error: none
# expect.trailing: 0
hex:
00 00 00 11                                       # length 17, u32 BE
2A 2A 44 50 54 4D 4F 50 43 2A 2A 00               # * * D P T M O P C * * \0
B1 B2 B3 B4 B5                                    # 5 trailing bytes (content unknown, #3; arbitrary)
